<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urho Kekkonen (1900–1986) was a Finnish politician of the Agrarian, later Centre, Party who served as prime minister five times and as president from 1956 to 1982, the longest presidency in Finnish history. He continued Paasikivi's policy of friendship with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, using his personal relations with Soviet leaders to secure room for trade with the West, but his long rule concentrated great power in the presidency and encouraged political self-censorship.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/urho-kekkonen.jpg" alt="Urho Kekkonen" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author / Kuvasiskot studio · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urho-Kekkonen-1975_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
